  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative or neutral and historical mean reversion is observed.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent upward spikes when sentiment is positive (e.g., >0.25) to avoid underestimating momentum.",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is significantly higher than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 5–10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp spikes by applying a smoothing factor (e.g., 0.85 multiplier) to prevent overcorrection.",
    "When sentiment is positive and forecast is below historical mean, increase forecast by 3–5% to align with bullish sentiment.",
    "If forecast consistently underperforms in high-sentiment periods, add a sentiment-weighted adjustment: forecast = base + sentiment * 0.15 * (true - forecast)."
  ]
}
